Those are not regular expressions. They're globs. A RegEx could be
"gr[ae]y" or ".*resist.*".

Do you mean the player enters a regex in the first place? That could be
easily detected by the special characters, so no need for the exact
search. Otherwise I don't see how the game should decide which parts of
the text it should generalize. Actually, I think the wish parser already
does some pretty decent guesswork as it is (for instance, it does accept
both gray and grey).

> matches in dialog boxes. User selects match he meant.  This will allow
> people to get their wish right even if they ask for it in a slightly
